#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm"
msgstr "Algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-algorithm.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"learning/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-algorithm.ipynb\" />\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Deutsch's algorithm outperforms all classical algorithms for a query problem, but the advantage is quite modest: one query versus two.\n"
"The Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm extends this advantage — and, in fact, it can be used to solve a couple of different query problems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma Deutsch mengungguli semua algoritma klasik untuk masalah query, tapi keuntungannya cukup kecil: satu query versus dua.\n"
"Algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa memperluas keuntungan ini — dan, sebenarnya, algoritma ini bisa digunakan untuk menyelesaikan beberapa masalah query yang berbeda.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's a quantum circuit description of the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm.\n"
"An additional classical post-processing step, not shown in the figure, may also be required depending on the specific problem being solved.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berikut deskripsi Circuit kuantum dari algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa.\n"
"Langkah pemrosesan klasik tambahan, yang tidak ditampilkan dalam gambar, mungkin juga diperlukan tergantung pada masalah spesifik yang sedang diselesaikan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Deutsch-Jozsa.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/Deutsch-Jozsa.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Of course, we haven't actually discussed what problems this algorithm solves; this is done in the two sections that follow.\n"
msgstr "Tentu saja, kita belum membahas masalah apa yang diselesaikan algoritma ini; hal itu dilakukan di dua bagian berikut.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Deutsch-Jozsa problem {#the-deutsch-jozsa-problem}"
msgstr "Masalah Deutsch-Jozsa {#the-deutsch-jozsa-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We'll begin with the query problem the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm was originally intended to solve, which is known as the *Deutsch-Jozsa problem*.\n"
msgstr "Kita akan mulai dengan masalah query yang awalnya dimaksudkan untuk diselesaikan oleh algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa, yang dikenal sebagai *masalah Deutsch-Jozsa*.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The input function for this problem takes the form $f:\\Sigma^n \\rightarrow \\Sigma$ for an arbitrary positive integer $n$.\n"
"Like Deutsch's problem, the task is to output $0$ if $f$ is constant and $1$ if $f$ is balanced, which again means that the number of input strings on which the function takes the value $0$ is equal to the number of input strings on which the function takes the value $1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fungsi input untuk masalah ini berbentuk $f:\\Sigma^n \\rightarrow \\Sigma$ untuk bilangan bulat positif $n$ yang sembarang.\n"
"Seperti masalah Deutsch, tugasnya adalah mengeluarkan $0$ jika $f$ konstan dan $1$ jika $f$ seimbang, yang kembali berarti bahwa jumlah string input di mana fungsi mengambil nilai $0$ sama dengan jumlah string input di mana fungsi mengambil nilai $1$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that, when $n$ is larger than $1$, there are functions of the form $f:\\Sigma^n \\rightarrow \\Sigma$ that are neither constant nor balanced.\n"
"For example, the function $f:\\Sigma^2\\rightarrow\\Sigma$ defined as\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa, ketika $n$ lebih besar dari $1$, ada fungsi berbentuk $f:\\Sigma^n \\rightarrow \\Sigma$ yang bukan konstan maupun seimbang.\n"
"Misalnya, fungsi $f:\\Sigma^2\\rightarrow\\Sigma$ yang didefinisikan sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"f(00) & = 0 \\\\\n"
"f(01) & = 0 \\\\\n"
"f(10) & = 0 \\\\\n"
"f(11) & = 1\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"f(00) & = 0 \\\\\n"
"f(01) & = 0 \\\\\n"
"f(10) & = 0 \\\\\n"
"f(11) & = 1\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"falls into neither of these two categories.\n"
"For the Deutsch-Jozsa problem, we simply don't worry about functions like this — they're considered to be \"don't care\" inputs.\n"
"That is, for this problem we have a *promise* that $f$ is either constant or balanced.\n"
msgstr ""
"tidak termasuk dalam salah satu dari dua kategori ini.\n"
"Untuk masalah Deutsch-Jozsa, kita tidak perlu khawatir tentang fungsi seperti ini — mereka dianggap sebagai input \"don't care\".\n"
"Artinya, untuk masalah ini kita memiliki *janji* bahwa $f$ adalah konstan atau seimbang.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Deutsch-Jozsa problem\">\n"
"Input: a function $f:\\{0,1\\}^n\\rightarrow\\{0,1\\}$ \\\n"
"Promise: $f$ is either constant or balanced \\\n"
"Output: $0$ if $f$ is constant, $1$ if $f$ is balanced\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Masalah Deutsch-Jozsa\">\n"
"Input: sebuah fungsi $f:\\{0,1\\}^n\\rightarrow\\{0,1\\}$ \\\n"
"Janji: $f$ adalah konstan atau seimbang \\\n"
"Output: $0$ jika $f$ konstan, $1$ jika $f$ seimbang\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm, with its single query, solves this problem in the following sense:\n"
"if every one of the $n$ measurement outcomes is $0$, then the function $f$ is constant;\n"
"and otherwise, if at least one of the measurement outcomes is $1$, then the function $f$ is balanced.\n"
"Another way to say this is that the circuit described above is followed by a classical post-processing step in which the OR of the measurement outcomes is computed to produce the output bit of the Deutsch-Jozsa problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa, dengan satu querynya, menyelesaikan masalah ini dalam pengertian berikut:\n"
"jika setiap satu dari $n$ hasil pengukuran adalah $0$, maka fungsi $f$ adalah konstan;\n"
"dan sebaliknya, jika setidaknya satu dari hasil pengukuran adalah $1$, maka fungsi $f$ adalah seimbang.\n"
"Cara lain untuk mengatakannya adalah bahwa Circuit yang dijelaskan di atas diikuti oleh langkah pemrosesan klasik di mana OR dari hasil pengukuran dihitung untuk menghasilkan output bit dari masalah Deutsch-Jozsa.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Algorithm analysis {#algorithm-analysis}"
msgstr "Analisis algoritma {#algorithm-analysis}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To analyze the performance of the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm for the Deutsch-Jozsa problem, it's helpful to begin by thinking about the action of a single layer of Hadamard gates.\n"
"A Hadamard operation can be expressed as a matrix in the usual way,\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menganalisis kinerja algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa untuk masalah Deutsch-Jozsa, ada baiknya kita mulai dengan memikirkan aksi dari satu lapisan Gate Hadamard.\n"
"Operasi Hadamard dapat diekspresikan sebagai matriks dengan cara biasa,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "but we can also express this operation in terms of its action on standard basis states:\n"
msgstr "tapi kita juga bisa mengekspresikan operasi ini dalam hal aksinya pada keadaan basis standar:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"H \\vert 0\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle\\\\[3mm]\n"
"H \\vert 1\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"H \\vert 0\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle\\\\[3mm]\n"
"H \\vert 1\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These two equations can be combined into a single formula,\n"
msgstr "Kedua persamaan ini dapat digabungkan menjadi satu rumus tunggal,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H \\vert a \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} (-1)^a \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\sum_{b\\in\\{0,1\\}} (-1)^{ab} \\vert b\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H \\vert a \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} (-1)^a \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\sum_{b\\in\\{0,1\\}} (-1)^{ab} \\vert b\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which is true for both choices of $a\\in\\Sigma$.\n"
msgstr "yang berlaku untuk kedua pilihan $a\\in\\Sigma$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now suppose that instead of just a single qubit we have $n$ qubits, and a Hadamard operation is performed on each.\n"
"The combined operation on the $n$ qubits is described by the tensor product $H\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes H$ ($n$ times), which we write as $H^{\\otimes n}$ for conciseness and clarity.\n"
"Using the formula from above, followed by expanding and then simplifying, we can express the action of this combined operation on the standard basis states of $n$ qubits like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang misalkan alih-alih hanya satu qubit kita punya $n$ qubit, dan operasi Hadamard dilakukan pada masing-masing.\n"
"Operasi gabungan pada $n$ qubit dijelaskan oleh produk tensor $H\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes H$ ($n$ kali), yang kita tulis sebagai $H^{\\otimes n}$ untuk keringkasan dan kejelasan.\n"
"Menggunakan rumus dari atas, dilanjutkan dengan mengekspansi kemudian menyederhanakan, kita dapat mengekspresikan aksi dari operasi gabungan ini pada keadaan basis standar dari $n$ qubit seperti ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  & H^{\\otimes n} \\vert x_{n-1} \\cdots x_1 x_0 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\bigl(H \\vert x_{n-1} \\rangle \\bigr) \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes \\bigl(H \\vert x_{0} \\rangle \\bigr) \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\Biggl( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\sum_{y_{n-1}\\in\\Sigma} (-1)^{x_{n-1} y_{n-1}} \\vert y_{n-1} \\rangle \\Biggr)\n"
"  \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\n"
"  \\Biggl( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\sum_{y_{0}\\in\\Sigma} (-1)^{x_{0} y_{0}} \\vert y_{0} \\rangle \\Biggr) \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"  (-1)^{x_{n-1}y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0} \\vert y_{n-1} \\cdots y_0 \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  & H^{\\otimes n} \\vert x_{n-1} \\cdots x_1 x_0 \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\bigl(H \\vert x_{n-1} \\rangle \\bigr) \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes \\bigl(H \\vert x_{0} \\rangle \\bigr) \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\Biggl( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\sum_{y_{n-1}\\in\\Sigma} (-1)^{x_{n-1} y_{n-1}} \\vert y_{n-1} \\rangle \\Biggr)\n"
"  \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\n"
"  \\Biggl( \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\sum_{y_{0}\\in\\Sigma} (-1)^{x_{0} y_{0}} \\vert y_{0} \\rangle \\Biggr) \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"  (-1)^{x_{n-1}y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0} \\vert y_{n-1} \\cdots y_0 \\rangle.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, by the way, we're writing binary strings of length $n$ as $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0$ and $y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0$, following Qiskit's indexing convention.\n"
msgstr "Di sini, ngomong-ngomong, kita menulis string biner panjang $n$ sebagai $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0$ dan $y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0$, mengikuti konvensi pengindeksan Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This formula provides us with a useful tool for analyzing the quantum circuit above.\n"
"After the first layer of Hadamard gates is performed, the state of the $n+1$ qubits (including the leftmost/bottom qubit, which is treated separately from the rest) is\n"
msgstr ""
"Rumus ini memberi kita alat yang berguna untuk menganalisis Circuit kuantum di atas.\n"
"Setelah lapisan pertama Gate Hadamard dilakukan, keadaan $n+1$ qubit (termasuk qubit paling kiri/bawah, yang diperlakukan secara terpisah dari yang lain) adalah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl( H \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\bigl( H^{\\otimes n} \\vert 0 \\cdots 0 \\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"= \\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n} \\vert x_{n-1} \\cdots x_0 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl( H \\vert 1 \\rangle \\bigr) \\bigl( H^{\\otimes n} \\vert 0 \\cdots 0 \\rangle \\bigr)\n"
"= \\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n} \\vert x_{n-1} \\cdots x_0 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When the $U_f$ operation is performed, this state is transformed into\n"
msgstr "Ketika operasi $U_f$ dilakukan, keadaan ini diubah menjadi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}}\n"
"\\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0)} \\vert x_{n-1} \\cdots x_0 \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}}\n"
"\\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0)} \\vert x_{n-1} \\cdots x_0 \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "through exactly the same phase kick-back phenomenon that we saw in the analysis of Deutsch's algorithm.\n"
msgstr "melalui fenomena phase kick-back yang persis sama seperti yang kita lihat dalam analisis algoritma Deutsch.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then the second layer of Hadamard gates is performed, which (by the formula above) transforms this state into\n"
msgstr "Kemudian lapisan kedua Gate Hadamard dilakukan, yang (berdasarkan rumus di atas) mengubah keadaan ini menjadi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"\\sum_{y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"(-1)^{f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0) + x_{n-1}y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0}\n"
"\\vert y_{n-1} \\cdots y_0 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"\\sum_{y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"(-1)^{f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0) + x_{n-1}y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0}\n"
"\\vert y_{n-1} \\cdots y_0 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This expression looks somewhat complicated, and not too much can be concluded about the probabilities to obtain different measurement outcomes without knowing more about the function $f$.\n"
msgstr "Ekspresi ini terlihat agak rumit, dan tidak banyak yang bisa disimpulkan tentang probabilitas untuk mendapatkan hasil pengukuran yang berbeda tanpa mengetahui lebih banyak tentang fungsi $f$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Fortunately, all we need to know is the probability that every one of the measurement outcomes is $0$ — because that's the probability that the algorithm determines that $f$ is constant.\n"
"This probability has a simple formula.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untungnya, yang perlu kita ketahui hanyalah probabilitas bahwa setiap satu dari hasil pengukuran adalah $0$ — karena itulah probabilitas bahwa algoritma menentukan bahwa $f$ adalah konstan.\n"
"Probabilitas ini memiliki rumus sederhana.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Biggl\\vert\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"(-1)^{f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0)}\n"
"\\Biggr\\vert^2\n"
"= \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & \\text{if $f$ is constant}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & \\text{if $f$ is balanced}\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Biggl\\vert\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 \\in \\Sigma^n}\n"
"(-1)^{f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0)}\n"
"\\Biggr\\vert^2\n"
"= \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & \\text{if $f$ is constant}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & \\text{if $f$ is balanced}\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that these values correspond to the probability of measuring the state\n"
"$\\vert 0^{\\otimes n} \\rangle$, rather than directly to the final classical output bit of\n"
"the Deutsch-Jozsa problem. The algorithm outputs $0$ when all measurement\n"
"outcomes are $0$ (indicating that $f$ is constant), and outputs $1$ otherwise\n"
"(indicating that $f$ is balanced).\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In greater detail, if $f$ is constant, then either $f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0) = 0$ for every string $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0$,\n"
"in which case the value of the sum is $2^n$, or $f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0) = 1$ for every string $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0$,\n"
"in which case the value of the sum is $-2^n$.\n"
"Dividing by $2^n$ and taking the square of the absolute value yields $1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lebih rinci, jika $f$ konstan, maka entah $f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0) = 0$ untuk setiap string $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0$,\n"
"dalam hal ini nilai jumlahnya adalah $2^n$, atau $f(x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0) = 1$ untuk setiap string $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0$,\n"
"dalam hal ini nilai jumlahnya adalah $-2^n$.\n"
"Membagi dengan $2^n$ dan mengambil kuadrat dari nilai absolut menghasilkan $1$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If, on the other hand, $f$ is balanced, then $f$ takes the value $0$ on half of the strings $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0$ and the value $1$ on the other half, so the $+1$ terms and $-1$ terms in the sum cancel and we're left with the value $0$.\n"
msgstr "Di sisi lain, jika $f$ seimbang, maka $f$ mengambil nilai $0$ pada setengah dari string $x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0$ dan nilai $1$ pada setengah lainnya, sehingga suku-suku $+1$ dan $-1$ dalam jumlah saling menghilangkan dan kita mendapat nilai $0.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We conclude that the algorithm operates correctly provided that the promise is fulfilled.\n"
msgstr "Kita menyimpulkan bahwa algoritma beroperasi dengan benar asalkan janji terpenuhi.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Classical difficulty {#classical-difficulty}"
msgstr "Kesulitan klasik {#classical-difficulty}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm works every time, always giving us the correct answer when the promise is met, and requires a single query.\n"
"How does this compare with classical query algorithms for the Deutsch-Jozsa problem?\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa bekerja setiap saat, selalu memberi kita jawaban yang benar ketika janji terpenuhi, dan hanya membutuhkan satu query.\n"
"Bagaimana ini dibandingkan dengan algoritma query klasik untuk masalah Deutsch-Jozsa?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, any *deterministic* classical algorithm that correctly solves the Deutsch-Jozsa problem must make exponentially many queries:\n"
"$2^{n-1} + 1$ queries are required in the worst case.\n"
"The reasoning is that, if a deterministic algorithm queries $f$ on $2^{n-1}$ or fewer different strings, and obtains the same function value every time, then both answers are still possible.\n"
"The function might be constant, or it might be balanced but through bad luck the queries all happen to return the same function value.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, algoritma klasik *deterministik* mana pun yang dengan benar menyelesaikan masalah Deutsch-Jozsa harus membuat query dalam jumlah eksponensial:\n"
"$2^{n-1} + 1$ query diperlukan dalam kasus terburuk.\n"
"Alasannya adalah bahwa, jika sebuah algoritma deterministik melakukan query $f$ pada $2^{n-1}$ atau lebih sedikit string yang berbeda, dan mendapatkan nilai fungsi yang sama setiap saat, maka kedua jawaban masih mungkin.\n"
"Fungsinya mungkin konstan, atau mungkin seimbang tetapi karena kemalangan, query-query tersebut semuanya mengembalikan nilai fungsi yang sama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The second possibility might seem unlikely — but for deterministic algorithms there's no randomness or uncertainty, so they will fail systematically on certain functions.\n"
"We therefore have a significant advantage of quantum over classical algorithms in this regard.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kemungkinan kedua mungkin tampak tidak mungkin — tetapi untuk algoritma deterministik tidak ada keacakan atau ketidakpastian, sehingga mereka akan gagal secara sistematis pada fungsi-fungsi tertentu.\n"
"Oleh karena itu kita memiliki keuntungan yang signifikan dari algoritma kuantum dibandingkan algoritma klasik dalam hal ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There is a catch, however, which is that *probabilistic* classical algorithms can solve the Deutsch-Jozsa problem with very high probability using just a few queries.\n"
"In particular, if we simply choose a few different strings of length $n$ randomly, and query $f$ on those strings, it's unlikely that we'll get the same function value for all of them when $f$ is balanced.\n"
msgstr ""
"Namun ada kendala, yaitu algoritma klasik *probabilistik* dapat menyelesaikan masalah Deutsch-Jozsa dengan probabilitas sangat tinggi hanya menggunakan beberapa query.\n"
"Khususnya, jika kita hanya memilih beberapa string berbeda panjang $n$ secara acak, dan melakukan query $f$ pada string-string tersebut, tidak mungkin kita mendapatkan nilai fungsi yang sama untuk semuanya ketika $f$ seimbang.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be specific, if we choose $k$ input strings $x^1,\\ldots,x^k \\in \\Sigma^n$ uniformly at random, evaluate $f(x^1),\\ldots,f(x^k)$, and answer $0$ if the function values are all the same, and $1$ if not, then we'll always be correct when $f$ is constant, and wrong in the case that $f$ is balanced with probability just $2^{-k + 1}$.\n"
"If we take $k = 11$, for instance, this algorithm will answer correctly with probability greater than $99.9$%.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lebih spesifik, jika kita memilih $k$ string input $x^1,\\ldots,x^k \\in \\Sigma^n$ secara seragam secara acak, mengevaluasi $f(x^1),\\ldots,f(x^k)$, dan menjawab $0$ jika nilai fungsinya semua sama, dan $1$ jika tidak, maka kita akan selalu benar ketika $f$ konstan, dan salah dalam kasus bahwa $f$ seimbang dengan probabilitas hanya $2^{-k + 1}$.\n"
"Jika kita mengambil $k = 11$, misalnya, algoritma ini akan menjawab dengan benar dengan probabilitas lebih besar dari $99.9$%.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For this reason, we do still have a rather modest advantage of quantum over classical algorithms — but it is nevertheless a quantifiable advantage representing an improvement over Deutsch's algorithm.\n"
msgstr "Karena alasan ini, kita tetap memiliki keuntungan yang cukup kecil dari kuantum dibandingkan algoritma klasik — tetapi tetap saja merupakan keuntungan yang dapat dikuantifikasi yang mewakili peningkatan atas algoritma Deutsch.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Deutsch-Jozsa with Qiskit {#deutsch-jozsa-with-qiskit}"
msgstr "Deutsch-Jozsa dengan Qiskit {#deutsch-jozsa-with-qiskit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To implement the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm in Qiskit, we'll start by defining a function `dj_query` that generates a quantum circuit implementing a query gate, for a randomly selected function satisfying the promise for the Deutsch-Jozsa problem.\n"
"With a 50% chance, the function is constant, and with 50% change the function is balanced.\n"
"For each of those two possibilities, the function is selected uniformly from the functions of that type.\n"
"The argument is the number of input bits of the function.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk mengimplementasikan algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa di Qiskit, kita akan mulai dengan mendefinisikan fungsi `dj_query` yang menghasilkan Circuit kuantum yang mengimplementasikan Gate query, untuk fungsi yang dipilih secara acak yang memenuhi janji untuk masalah Deutsch-Jozsa.\n"
"Dengan peluang 50%, fungsinya konstan, dan dengan peluang 50% fungsinya seimbang.\n"
"Untuk masing-masing dari dua kemungkinan tersebut, fungsinya dipilih secara seragam dari fungsi-fungsi dengan tipe tersebut.\n"
"Argumennya adalah jumlah bit input dari fungsi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can show the quantum circuit implementation of the query gate using the `draw` method as usual.\n"
msgstr "Kita dapat menampilkan implementasi Circuit kuantum dari Gate query menggunakan metode `draw` seperti biasa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-algorithm/extracted-outputs/b4a6df3d-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-algorithm/extracted-outputs/b4a6df3d-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next we define a function that creates the Deutsch-Jozsa circuit, taking a quantum circuit implementation of a query gate as an argument.\n"
msgstr "Selanjutnya kita mendefinisikan fungsi yang membuat Circuit Deutsch-Jozsa, dengan mengambil implementasi Circuit kuantum dari Gate query sebagai argumen.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, a function that runs the Deutsch-Jozsa circuit once is defined.\n"
msgstr "Terakhir, sebuah fungsi yang menjalankan Circuit Deutsch-Jozsa sekali didefinisikan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can test our implementation by choosing a function randomly, displaying the quantum circuit implementation of a query gate for this function, and then running the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm on that function.\n"
msgstr "Kita dapat menguji implementasi kita dengan memilih fungsi secara acak, menampilkan implementasi Circuit kuantum dari Gate query untuk fungsi ini, lalu menjalankan algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa pada fungsi tersebut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-algorithm/extracted-outputs/aca4745e-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-algorithm/extracted-outputs/aca4745e-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Bernstein-Vazirani problem {#the-bernstein-vazirani-problem}"
msgstr "Masalah Bernstein-Vazirani {#the-bernstein-vazirani-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we'll discuss a problem known as the *Bernstein-Vazirani problem*.\n"
"It's also called the *Fourier sampling problem*, although there are more general formulations of this problem that also go by that name.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selanjutnya, kita akan membahas masalah yang dikenal sebagai *masalah Bernstein-Vazirani*.\n"
"Ini juga disebut *masalah Fourier sampling*, meskipun ada formulasi yang lebih umum dari masalah ini yang juga menggunakan nama tersebut.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, let's introduce some notation.\n"
"For any two binary strings $x = x_{n-1} \\cdots x_0$ and $y = y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0$ of length $n$, we define\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, mari kita perkenalkan beberapa notasi.\n"
"Untuk dua string biner $x = x_{n-1} \\cdots x_0$ dan $y = y_{n-1}\\cdots y_0$ dengan panjang $n$, kita mendefinisikan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"x \\cdot y = x_{n-1} y_{n-1} \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus x_0 y_0.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"x \\cdot y = x_{n-1} y_{n-1} \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus x_0 y_0.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll refer to this operation as the *binary dot product*.\n"
"An alternative way to define it is like so.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan menyebut operasi ini sebagai *produk titik biner*.\n"
"Cara alternatif untuk mendefinisikannya adalah seperti ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"x \\cdot y =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & x_{{n-1}} y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0 \\text{ is odd}\\\\[0.5mm]\n"
"0 & x_{{n-1}} y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0 \\text{ is even}\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"x \\cdot y =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & x_{{n-1}} y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0 \\text{ is odd}\\\\[0.5mm]\n"
"0 & x_{{n-1}} y_{n-1} + \\cdots + x_0 y_0 \\text{ is even}\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that this is a symmetric operation, meaning that the result doesn't change if we swap $x$ and $y$, so we're free to do that whenever it's convenient.\n"
"Sometimes it's useful to think about the binary dot product $x \\cdot y$ as being the parity of the bits of $x$ in positions where the string $y$ has a $1$, or equivalently, the parity of the bits of $y$ in positions where the string $x$ has a $1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa ini adalah operasi simetris, artinya hasilnya tidak berubah jika kita menukar $x$ dan $y$, jadi kita bebas melakukan itu kapan saja ketika itu nyaman.\n"
"Terkadang berguna untuk memikirkan produk titik biner $x \\cdot y$ sebagai paritas bit dari $x$ di posisi di mana string $y$ memiliki $1$, atau secara ekivalen, paritas bit dari $y$ di posisi di mana string $x$ memiliki $1$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With this notation in hand we can now define the Bernstein-Vazirani problem.\n"
msgstr "Dengan notasi ini di tangan, kita sekarang dapat mendefinisikan masalah Bernstein-Vazirani.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Bernstein-Vazirani problem\">\n"
"Input: a function $f:\\{0,1\\}^n\\rightarrow\\{0,1\\}$ \\\n"
"Promise: there exists a binary string $s = s_{n-1} \\cdots s_0$ for which $f(x) = s\\cdot x$ for all $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ \\\n"
"Output: the string $s$\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Masalah Bernstein-Vazirani\">\n"
"Input: sebuah fungsi $f:\\{0,1\\}^n\\rightarrow\\{0,1\\}$ \\\n"
"Janji: ada string biner $s = s_{n-1} \\cdots s_0$ di mana $f(x) = s\\cdot x$ untuk semua $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ \\\n"
"Output: string $s$\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We don't actually need a new quantum algorithm for this problem; the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm solves it.\n"
"In the interest of clarity, let's refer to the quantum circuit from above, which doesn't include the classical post-processing step of computing the OR, as the *Deutsch-Jozsa circuit*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita sebenarnya tidak membutuhkan algoritma kuantum baru untuk masalah ini; algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa menyelesaikannya.\n"
"Demi kejelasan, mari kita sebut Circuit kuantum dari atas, yang tidak mencakup langkah pemrosesan klasik berupa komputasi OR, sebagai *Circuit Deutsch-Jozsa*.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Algorithm analysis {#algorithm-analysis-1}"
msgstr "Analisis algoritma {#algorithm-analysis-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To analyze how the Deutsch-Jozsa circuit works for a function satisfying the promise for the Bernstein-Vazirani problem, we'll begin with a quick observation.\n"
"Using the binary dot product, we can alternatively describe the action of $n$ Hadamard gates on the standard basis states of $n$ qubits as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menganalisis bagaimana Circuit Deutsch-Jozsa bekerja untuk fungsi yang memenuhi janji untuk masalah Bernstein-Vazirani, kita akan mulai dengan pengamatan singkat.\n"
"Menggunakan produk titik biner, kita dapat secara alternatif mendeskripsikan aksi dari $n$ Gate Hadamard pada keadaan basis standar dari $n$ qubit sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes n} \\vert x \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{y\\in\\Sigma^n} (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\vert y\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H^{\\otimes n} \\vert x \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{y\\in\\Sigma^n} (-1)^{x\\cdot y} \\vert y\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Similar to what we saw when analyzing Deutsch's algorithm, this is because the value $(-1)^k$ for any integer $k$ depends only on whether $k$ is even or odd.\n"
msgstr "Mirip dengan yang kita lihat ketika menganalisis algoritma Deutsch, ini karena nilai $(-1)^k$ untuk bilangan bulat $k$ apa pun hanya bergantung pada apakah $k$ genap atau ganjil.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Turning to the Deutsch–Jozsa circuit, after the first layer of Hadamard gates is performed, the state of the $n+1$ qubits is\n"
msgstr "Beralih ke Circuit Deutsch-Jozsa, setelah lapisan pertama Gate Hadamard dilakukan, keadaan $n+1$ qubit adalah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\vert x \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\vert x \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The query gate is then performed, which (through the phase kickback phenomenon) transforms the state into\n"
msgstr "Gate query kemudian dilakukan, yang (melalui fenomena phase kickback) mengubah keadaan menjadi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{f(x)} \\vert x \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^n}} \\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{f(x)} \\vert x \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using our formula for the action of a layer of Hadamard gates, we see that the second layer of Hadamard gates then transforms this state into\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan rumus kita untuk aksi dari lapisan Gate Hadamard, kita melihat bahwa lapisan kedua Gate Hadamard kemudian mengubah keadaan ini menjadi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{f(x) + x \\cdot y} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{f(x) + x \\cdot y} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we can make some simplifications, in the exponent of $-1$ inside the sum.\n"
"We're promised that $f(x) = s\\cdot x$ for some string $s = s_{n-1} \\cdots s_0$, so we can express the state as\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang kita dapat membuat beberapa penyederhanaan, dalam eksponen $-1$ di dalam jumlah.\n"
"Kita dijanjikan bahwa $f(x) = s\\cdot x$ untuk suatu string $s = s_{n-1} \\cdots s_0$, jadi kita dapat mengekspresikan keadaan sebagai\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{s\\cdot x + x \\cdot y} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{s\\cdot x + x \\cdot y} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because $s\\cdot x$ and $x\\cdot y$ are binary values, we can replace the addition with the exclusive-OR — again because the only thing that matters for an integer in the exponent of $-1$ is whether it is even or odd.\n"
"Making use of the symmetry of the binary dot product, we obtain this expression for the state:\n"
msgstr ""
"Karena $s\\cdot x$ dan $x\\cdot y$ adalah nilai biner, kita dapat mengganti penjumlahan dengan eksklusif-OR — kembali karena satu-satunya hal yang penting untuk bilangan bulat dalam eksponen $-1$ adalah apakah itu genap atau ganjil.\n"
"Memanfaatkan simetri produk titik biner, kita mendapatkan ekspresi berikut untuk keadaan:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{(s\\cdot x) \\oplus (y \\cdot x)} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{(s\\cdot x) \\oplus (y \\cdot x)} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "(Parentheses have been added for clarity, though they aren't really necessary because it's conventional to treat the binary dot product as having higher precedence than the exclusive-OR.)\n"
msgstr "(Tanda kurung telah ditambahkan untuk kejelasan, meskipun sebenarnya tidak diperlukan karena konvensinya adalah memperlakukan produk titik biner sebagai memiliki prioritas lebih tinggi dari eksklusif-OR.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At this point we will make use of the following formula.\n"
msgstr "Pada titik ini kita akan memanfaatkan rumus berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(s\\cdot x) \\oplus (y \\cdot x) = (s \\oplus y) \\cdot x\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(s\\cdot x) \\oplus (y \\cdot x) = (s \\oplus y) \\cdot x\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can obtain the formula through a similar formula for bits,\n"
msgstr "Kita dapat memperoleh rumus ini melalui rumus serupa untuk bit,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(a c) \\oplus (b c) = (a \\oplus b) c,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(a c) \\oplus (b c) = (a \\oplus b) c,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "together with an expansion of the binary dot product and bitwise exclusive-OR:\n"
msgstr "bersama dengan ekspansi produk titik biner dan eksklusif-OR bitwise:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(s\\cdot x) \\oplus (y \\cdot x)\n"
"& = (s_{n-1} x_{n-1}) \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus (s_{0} x_{0}) \\oplus\n"
"(y_{n-1} x_{n-1})  \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus (y_{0} x_{0}) \\\\\n"
"& = (s_{n-1} \\oplus y_{n-1}) x_{n-1}  \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus (s_{0} \\oplus y_{0}) x_{0} \\\\\n"
"& = (s \\oplus y) \\cdot x\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(s\\cdot x) \\oplus (y \\cdot x)\n"
"& = (s_{n-1} x_{n-1}) \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus (s_{0} x_{0}) \\oplus\n"
"(y_{n-1} x_{n-1})  \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus (y_{0} x_{0}) \\\\\n"
"& = (s_{n-1} \\oplus y_{n-1}) x_{n-1}  \\oplus \\cdots \\oplus (s_{0} \\oplus y_{0}) x_{0} \\\\\n"
"& = (s \\oplus y) \\cdot x\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This allows us to express the state of the circuit immediately prior to the measurements like this:\n"
msgstr "Ini memungkinkan kita untuk mengekspresikan keadaan Circuit tepat sebelum pengukuran seperti ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{(s\\oplus y)\\cdot x} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{(s\\oplus y)\\cdot x} \\vert y \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The final step is to make use of yet another formula, which works for every binary string $z = z_{n-1}\\cdots z_0$.\n"
msgstr "Langkah terakhir adalah memanfaatkan satu rumus lagi, yang berlaku untuk setiap string biner $z = z_{n-1}\\cdots z_0$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{z \\cdot x}\n"
"= \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & \\text{if $z = 0^n$}\\\\\n"
"0 & \\text{if $z\\neq 0^n$}\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{z \\cdot x}\n"
"= \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & \\text{if $z = 0^n$}\\\\\n"
"0 & \\text{if $z\\neq 0^n$}\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we're using a simple notation for strings that we'll use several more times in the lesson: $0^n$ is the all-zero string of length $n$.\n"
msgstr "Di sini kita menggunakan notasi sederhana untuk string yang akan kita gunakan beberapa kali lagi dalam pelajaran ini: $0^n$ adalah string semua-nol dengan panjang $n.$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A simple way to argue that this formula works is to consider the two cases separately.\n"
"If $z = 0^n$, then $z\\cdot x = 0$ for every string $x\\in\\Sigma^n$, so the value of each term in the sum is $1$, and we obtain $1$ by summing and dividing by $2^n$.\n"
"On the other hand, if any one of the bits of $z$ is equal to $1$, then the binary dot product $z\\cdot x$ is equal to $0$ for exactly half of the possible choices for $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ and $1$ for the other half — because the value of the binary dot product $z\\cdot x$ flips (from $0$ to $1$ or from $1$ to $0$) if we flip any bit of $x$ in a position where $z$ has a $1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cara sederhana untuk menunjukkan bahwa rumus ini berlaku adalah dengan mempertimbangkan dua kasus secara terpisah.\n"
"Jika $z = 0^n$, maka $z\\cdot x = 0$ untuk setiap string $x\\in\\Sigma^n$, sehingga nilai setiap suku dalam jumlah adalah $1$, dan kita mendapatkan $1$ dengan menjumlahkan dan membagi dengan $2^n$.\n"
"Di sisi lain, jika salah satu bit dari $z$ sama dengan $1$, maka produk titik biner $z\\cdot x$ sama dengan $0$ untuk tepat setengah dari kemungkinan pilihan $x\\in\\Sigma^n$ dan $1$ untuk setengah lainnya — karena nilai produk titik biner $z\\cdot x$ berbalik (dari $0$ ke $1$ atau dari $1$ ke $0$) jika kita membalik bit apa pun dari $x$ di posisi di mana $z$ memiliki $1$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we now apply this formula to simplify the state of the circuit prior to the measurements, we obtain\n"
msgstr "Jika kita sekarang menerapkan rumus ini untuk menyederhanakan keadaan Circuit sebelum pengukuran, kita mendapatkan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{(s\\oplus y)\\cdot x} \\vert y \\rangle\n"
"= \\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\vert s \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\frac{1}{2^n}\n"
"\\sum_{x \\in \\Sigma^n} \\sum_{y \\in \\Sigma^n} (-1)^{(s\\oplus y)\\cdot x} \\vert y \\rangle\n"
"= \\vert - \\rangle \\otimes \\vert s \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"owing to the fact that $s\\oplus y = 0^n$ if and only if $y = s$.\n"
"Thus, the measurements reveal precisely the string $s$ we're looking for.\n"
msgstr ""
"karena $s\\oplus y = 0^n$ jika dan hanya jika $y = s$.\n"
"Dengan demikian, pengukuran mengungkapkan tepat string $s$ yang kita cari.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Classical difficulty {#classical-difficulty-1}"
msgstr "Kesulitan klasik {#classical-difficulty-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "While the Deutsch-Jozsa circuit solves the Bernstein-Vazirani problem with a single query, any classical query algorithm must make at least $n$ queries to solve this problem.\n"
msgstr "Sementara Circuit Deutsch-Jozsa menyelesaikan masalah Bernstein-Vazirani dengan satu query, algoritma query klasik mana pun harus membuat setidaknya $n$ query untuk menyelesaikan masalah ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This can be reasoned through a so-called *information theoretic* argument, which is very simple in this case.\n"
"Each classical query reveals a single bit of information about the solution, and there are $n$ bits of information that need to be uncovered — so at least $n$ queries are needed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hal ini dapat dibuktikan melalui argumen yang disebut *information theoretic*, yang sangat sederhana dalam kasus ini.\n"
"Setiap query klasik mengungkapkan satu bit informasi tentang solusi, dan ada $n$ bit informasi yang perlu diungkap — sehingga setidaknya $n$ query diperlukan.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is, in fact, possible to solve the Bernstein-Vazirani problem classically by querying the function on each of the $n$ strings having a single $1$, in each possible position, and $0$ for all other bits, which reveals the bits of $s$ one at a time.\n"
"Therefore, the advantage of quantum over classical algorithms for this problem is $1$ query versus $n$ queries.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebenarnya, memang mungkin untuk menyelesaikan masalah Bernstein-Vazirani secara klasik dengan melakukan query fungsi pada masing-masing dari $n$ string yang memiliki satu $1$, di setiap posisi yang mungkin, dan $0$ untuk semua bit lainnya, yang mengungkapkan bit-bit dari $s$ satu per satu.\n"
"Oleh karena itu, keuntungan kuantum dibandingkan algoritma klasik untuk masalah ini adalah $1$ query versus $n$ query.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bernstein-Vazirani with Qiskit {#bernstein-vazirani-with-qiskit}"
msgstr "Bernstein-Vazirani dengan Qiskit {#bernstein-vazirani-with-qiskit}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We've already implemented the Deutsch-Jozsa circuit above, and here we will make use of it to solve the Bernstein-Vazirani problem.\n"
"First we'll define a function that implements a query gate for the Bernstein-Vazirani problem given any binary string $s$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita sudah mengimplementasikan Circuit Deutsch-Jozsa di atas, dan di sini kita akan menggunakannya untuk menyelesaikan masalah Bernstein-Vazirani.\n"
"Pertama kita akan mendefinisikan fungsi yang mengimplementasikan Gate query untuk masalah Bernstein-Vazirani untuk string biner $s$ apa pun.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-algorithm/extracted-outputs/11861a7e-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/fundamentals-of-quantum-algorithms/quantum-query-algorithms/deutsch-jozsa-algorithm/extracted-outputs/11861a7e-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we can create a function that runs the Deutsch-Jozsa circuit on the function, using the `compile_circuit` function that was defined previously.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita dapat membuat fungsi yang menjalankan Circuit Deutsch-Jozsa pada fungsi tersebut, menggunakan fungsi `compile_circuit` yang telah didefinisikan sebelumnya.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remark on nomenclature {#remark-on-nomenclature}"
msgstr "Catatan tentang nomenklatur {#remark-on-nomenclature}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the context of the Bernstein-Vazirani problem, it is common that the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm is referred to as the \"Bernstein-Vazirani algorithm.\"\n"
"This is slightly misleading, because the algorithm *is* the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm, as Bernstein and Vazirani were very clear about in their work.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam konteks masalah Bernstein-Vazirani, umum bahwa algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa disebut sebagai \"algoritma Bernstein-Vazirani.\"\n"
"Ini sedikit menyesatkan, karena algoritmanya *adalah* algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa, seperti yang sangat jelas dikatakan oleh Bernstein dan Vazirani dalam karya mereka.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What Bernstein and Vazirani did after showing that the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm solves the Bernstein-Vazirani problem (as it is stated above) was to define a much more complicated problem, known as the *recursive Fourier sampling problem*.\n"
"This is a highly contrived problem where solutions to different instances of the problem effectively unlock new levels of the problem arranged in a tree-like structure.\n"
"The Bernstein-Vazirani problem is essentially just the base case of this more complicated problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Yang Bernstein dan Vazirani lakukan setelah menunjukkan bahwa algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa menyelesaikan masalah Bernstein-Vazirani (seperti yang dinyatakan di atas) adalah mendefinisikan masalah yang jauh lebih rumit, yang dikenal sebagai *masalah recursive Fourier sampling*.\n"
"Ini adalah masalah yang sangat dibuat-buat di mana solusi untuk instance yang berbeda dari masalah tersebut secara efektif membuka level baru dari masalah yang disusun dalam struktur seperti pohon.\n"
"Masalah Bernstein-Vazirani pada dasarnya hanyalah kasus dasar dari masalah yang lebih rumit ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The recursive Fourier sampling problem was the first known example of a query problem where quantum algorithms have a so-called *super-polynomial* advantage over probabilistic algorithms, thereby surpassing the advantage of quantum over classical offered by the Deutsch-Jozsa algorithm.\n"
"Intuitively speaking, the recursive version of the problem amplifies the $1$ versus $n$ advantage of quantum algorithms to something much larger.\n"
msgstr ""
"Masalah recursive Fourier sampling adalah contoh pertama yang diketahui dari masalah query di mana algoritma kuantum memiliki keuntungan yang disebut *super-polinomial* atas algoritma probabilistik, sehingga melampaui keuntungan kuantum dibandingkan klasik yang ditawarkan oleh algoritma Deutsch-Jozsa.\n"
"Secara intuitif, versi rekursif dari masalah ini memperkuat keuntungan $1$ versus $n$ dari algoritma kuantum menjadi sesuatu yang jauh lebih besar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The most challenging aspect of the mathematical analysis establishing this advantage is showing that classical query algorithms can't solve the problem without making lots of queries.\n"
"This is quite typical; for many problems it can be very difficult to rule out creative classical approaches that solve them efficiently.\n"
msgstr ""
"Aspek paling menantang dari analisis matematika yang menetapkan keuntungan ini adalah menunjukkan bahwa algoritma query klasik tidak dapat menyelesaikan masalah tanpa membuat banyak query.\n"
"Ini sangat khas; untuk banyak masalah bisa sangat sulit untuk mengecualikan pendekatan klasik yang kreatif yang menyelesaikannya secara efisien.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Simon's problem, and the algorithm for it described in the next section, does provide a much simpler example of a super-polynomial (and, in fact, exponential) advantage of quantum over classical algorithms, and for this reason the recursive Fourier sampling problem is less often discussed.\n"
"It is, nevertheless, an interesting computational problem in its own right.\n"
msgstr ""
"Masalah Simon, dan algoritma untuk itu yang dijelaskan di bagian berikutnya, memang memberikan contoh yang jauh lebih sederhana dari keuntungan super-polinomial (dan, sebenarnya, eksponensial) kuantum dibandingkan algoritma klasik, dan karena alasan ini masalah recursive Fourier sampling lebih jarang dibahas.\n"
"Namun demikian, ini adalah masalah komputasi yang menarik dengan sendirinya.\n"
